# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Easyway LMS — environment template
#
# Copy this file to BOTH .env and .env.local, then fill in what you need:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Why both: Prisma (the CLI included) reads .env, while Next.js reads
# .env.local. DATABASE_URL has to be present in both or `prisma db push`
# and the running app will disagree about where the database lives.
#
# Only the REQUIRED block below is needed to boot the app. Every optional
# key degrades gracefully when missing — the related feature turns itself
# off rather than crashing, so a fresh clone always runs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- REQUIRED --------------------------------------------------------------

# Postgres, not SQLite. See DEPLOY.md for why, and for how to create a free
# database in about two minutes.
#
# TWO urls, and they are not interchangeable:
#   DATABASE_URL         the POOLED string. What the app uses. Every serverless
#                        request opens its own connection, so without a pooler
#                        a busy morning exhausts the server's connection limit
#                        and the whole school sees errors at once.
#   DIRECT_DATABASE_URL  the DIRECT string. What migrations use, because they
#                        cannot run through a pooler in transaction mode.
#
# Neon and Supabase both hand you the two. If your provider gives only one,
# set both to it and watch the connection count.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true"
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# Any long random string. Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
# In production this MUST be set and MUST NOT be the one from this file:
# it is what signs session cookies, and a known value lets anybody mint one.
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="replace-me-with-a-long-random-string"
# The site's own address. On Vercel this is the production domain, with https.
# Sign-in redirects break in confusing ways when it is wrong.
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXTAUTH_URL_INTERNAL="http://localhost:3000"


# --- OPTIONAL: payments ----------------------------------------------------
# Paystack handles tuition (NGN). Without these, checkout is unavailable but
# the rest of the app is unaffected.
PAYSTACK_SECRET_KEY=""
PAYSTACK_CALLBACK_URL="http://localhost:3000/api/paystack/callback"

# Stripe is legacy, used by the older pathway checkout only.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=""
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""


# --- OPTIONAL: email -------------------------------------------------------
# Set EMAIL_PROVIDER=zoho to use the school's Zoho mailbox — host and port are
# filled in for you and SMTP_PASS is a Zoho app-specific password, not the
# account password. Leave it blank to configure SMTP_* by hand.
#
# Zoho Mail's FREE plan does NOT allow SMTP (Zoho lists "IMAP/POP/Active Sync
# not included" on Forever Free) — it fails with 535 Authentication Failed.
# Either pay for Mail Lite (~$1/mailbox/month), or point SMTP_HOST at a
# transactional sender instead: ZeptoMail ($2.50/10k), Brevo (free, 300/day,
# smtp-relay.brevo.com:587) or Resend (free, 3k/month, smtp.resend.com:587).
# The zoho preset hardcodes smtp.zoho.com; .eu and .in accounts need SMTP_HOST.
EMAIL_PROVIDER="zoho"
# Welcome mails, fee reminders, exam reminders and graduation notices.
# WITHOUT SMTP_HOST the mailer skips delivery silently and only logs a
# warning — mail appears to "work" in the UI but nothing is ever sent.
SMTP_HOST=""
SMTP_PORT="587"
SMTP_SECURE="false"
SMTP_USER=""
SMTP_PASS=""
SMTP_FROM="Easyway LMS <no-reply@easyway.test>"


# --- OPTIONAL: MailerLite / MailerSend --------------------------------------
# Two products from the same company doing different jobs:
#
#   MailerLite (connect.mailerlite.com) — MARKETING. Subscribers, groups and
#   campaigns. It has no endpoint for sending one email to one person, so it
#   cannot carry a fee receipt or an exam confirmation.
#
#   MailerSend (api.mailersend.com) — TRANSACTIONAL. One message to one
#   recipient. This is what receipts, reminders and confirmations need, and it
#   takes its OWN key.
#
# The two keys are NOT interchangeable — using one against the other's API
# returns 401 "Unauthenticated", which reads like a bad key. Verify with:
#   node scripts/check-email.mjs
#
# When MAILERSEND_API_KEY is set it is used ahead of SMTP — an HTTP API needs
# no outbound port 587, which many hosts block.
MAILERLITE_API_KEY=""
MAILERSEND_API_KEY=""


# --- OPTIONAL: push notifications ------------------------------------------
# Generate a keypair with:  node scripts/generate-vapid-keys.mjs
# Push silently disables itself when these are absent.
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=""
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=""
VAPID_SUBJECT="mailto:you@example.com"


# --- OPTIONAL: AI ----------------------------------------------------------
# Lesson structuring, feedback and practice. Order tried: local Ollama, then
# Claude, then Groq, then DeepSeek, then canned mock responses — so this works
# with none set. On a machine/host with no local Ollama (RAM, or Vercel),
# GROQ_API_KEY is the fastest way to get real AI live: a free API key from
# console.groq.com, no server or monthly bill required.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL="http://127.0.0.1:11434"
OLLAMA_MODEL="mistral"
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
GROQ_API_KEY=""
OPENAI_API_KEY=""
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=""


# --- OPTIONAL: speech ------------------------------------------------------
# Pronunciation scoring. Without it, pronunciation practice is disabled.
AZURE_SPEECH_KEY=""
AZURE_SPEECH_REGION=""


# --- REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION: file storage -----------------------------------
# Where student photos, ID scans and course material are kept.
#
# On a laptop these can stay empty and files land in public/uploads. On Vercel
# they cannot: the filesystem there is read-only apart from /tmp, and /tmp
# belongs to a single request. An upload would either fail outright or appear
# to work and be gone moments later, which is the worse of the two.
#
# Any S3-compatible bucket. Cloudflare R2 is the recommendation — no egress
# charge, and one bucket can serve recordings too (the RECORDING_S3_* values
# below are read as a fallback, so you only need one set of credentials).
STORAGE_S3_BUCKET=""
STORAGE_S3_REGION="auto"
STORAGE_S3_ENDPOINT=""
STORAGE_S3_ACCESS_KEY=""
STORAGE_S3_SECRET=""

# LEAVE THIS EMPTY unless you mean it. Empty means uploads are served through
# /api/files, behind the session check. Setting it makes every stored file
# world-readable at a guessable URL — including passport scans.
STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=""


# --- OPTIONAL: class recording storage --------------------------------------
# Where captured live classes are written. Any S3-compatible bucket: Cloudflare
# R2 (recommended — zero egress fees), Backblaze B2, AWS S3, or MinIO.
# Without these, classes stream normally and are simply not recorded.
RECORDING_S3_BUCKET=""
RECORDING_S3_REGION="auto"
RECORDING_S3_ENDPOINT=""
RECORDING_S3_ACCESS_KEY=""
RECORDING_S3_SECRET=""
RECORDING_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=""

# Shared secret for the scheduler. Vercel Cron signs its own requests with
# this automatically once it is set here; /api/cron/tick refuses everybody
# while it is empty, because an open endpoint that drains a mail queue is a
# way to get the school's domain blacklisted.
CRON_SECRET=""

# "true" lets the scheduled run actually delete recordings the retention
# policy has finished with. Anything else and it only reports what it would
# reclaim. Look at that number before you turn this on.
RETENTION_AUTO=""

# --- Two-factor authentication (admin accounts) -------------------------
# "true" turns away admins who hold `payments` or `security` and have not
# enrolled. Leave this UNSET until every super admin has actually set up their
# authenticator: switching it on first locks them out of the very screen they
# would enrol on. See docs/SECURITY.md §10.
MFA_ENFORCED=""

# Encrypts the stored TOTP secrets at rest, so reading the database is not
# enough to mint codes. Falls back to NEXTAUTH_SECRET when empty — which works,
# but then rotating NEXTAUTH_SECRET silently invalidates every enrolment and
# the whole office has to set up again. Generate: openssl rand -base64 48
MFA_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

# --- Sending identities -----------------------------------------------------
# The school sends as TWO addresses from ONE authenticated mailbox. SMTP auth is
# per mailbox (SMTP_USER); the From: header is per message, which is what lets
# both of these work on a single plan. Both must be on a domain with SPF+DKIM
# set up for whichever provider you use, or the second one starts landing in
# spam while the first looks fine.
#
#   support    a person reads the replies — announcements, tutor messages
#   noreply    automated — receipts, results, confirmations
#
# Defaults are support@ and donotreply@ on MAIL_DOMAIN, so these are optional.
MAIL_DOMAIN="easywaylanguageschool.com"
MAIL_SCHOOL_NAME="Easyway Language School"
MAIL_SUPPORT_ADDRESS="support@easywaylanguageschool.com"
MAIL_NOREPLY_ADDRESS="donotreply@easywaylanguageschool.com"
